<div>
  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/minerssaa.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Cryptocurrencies have jumped quite a bit in value over the course of the year and miners who verify transactions and earn digital assets have seen significant profits. While bitcoin miners have been seeing daily profits rise, a great number of other mineable digital currencies are pulling in much larger yields. </strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Blake256R14 and Ethash Machines Pull Bigger Profits Than SHA256 Mining Devices
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    The overall valuation of all cryptocurrencies in existence is around $1.5 trillion as digital asset values have risen considerably in 2021. While a great number of blockchains leverage consensus algorithms like proof-of-stake (PoS), there’s plenty of coins that can be mined with a machine like an application-specific integrated circuit (ASIC) mining rig.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Mining rigs that can mine bitcoin (BTC) using the SHA256 algorithm can bring in anywhere between $7 to $16 per day in profits. That’s of course if the miner is using the latest hardware with at least 50 terahash per second (TH/s) of hashpower.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-463914 size-full" title="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake.jpg" alt="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" width="1280" height="250" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake-300x59.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake-1024x200.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake-768x150.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake-696x136.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/blake-1068x209.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Both Microbt and Bitmain produce the top BTC mining rigs on the market today because they pull in the most profits. Using today’s BTC mining difficulty and electricity costs — around $0.12 per kilowatt-hour (kWh) — the Bitmain Antminer S19 Pro and the Microbt Whatsminer M30S++ get around $16 per day in profits.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    While that’s good, some mining rigs that mine other types of crypto assets make considerably larger profits in comparison. One such example is decred (DCR), as a mining rig that processes the Blake256R14 algorithm can make between $40 to $50 per day.
  </p><figure id="attachment_463912" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-463912" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-463912 size-full" title="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth.jpg" alt="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" width="1280" height="170" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth-300x40.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth-1024x136.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth-768x102.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth-696x92.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/eth-1068x142.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-463912" class="wp-caption-text">Profit stats featured in this article stem from asicminervalue.com on June 4, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    The top two decred mining devices include the Strongu STU-U1++ and the Microbt Whatsminer D1. Microbt’s machine pulls 2,200 watts off the wall and produces around 48 TH/s in hashpower. Statistics indicate that the Strongu device also pulls 2,200 watts but produces about 52 TH/s.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Coins that can be mined with the consensus algorithm Ethash (ubiq, ethereum, ethereum classic, pirl, and callisto) show their mining rigs rake in significant profits as well. For instance, the Innosilicon A10 Pro+ ETH miner gets around 759 megahash per second (MH/s) and $50 a day in profit.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Equihash and Scrypt
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Following yields from Ethash, the consensus algorithm Equihash that mines coins like zcash, zencash, komodo and more, also sees profitable returns. The top mining rig that can dedicate hashrate to Equihash consensus is Bitmain’s Antminer Z15.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-463910 size-full" title="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash.jpg" alt="Alternative Mining Algorithms Reap Higher Profits Than Bitcoin Mining in 2021" width="1280" height="250" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash-300x59.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash-1024x200.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash-768x150.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash-696x136.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hash-1068x209.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The Antminer Z15 gets around $47 per day with its maximum hashrate of 420 ksol/s (solutions per second) and power consumption of around 1,510 watts. The second-best unit is a step down from Bitmain’s powerful Equihash miner — Innosilicon’s A9++ Zmaster. It does around 140 ksol/s and only pulls in $11 per day.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Still, the Zmaster does better than a majority of SHA256 miners that mine BTC. Even litecoin (LTC) miners will produce better profits by mining Scrypt. At the time of publication, the Innosilicon A6+ Ltcmaster and the lower-end A6 are the top two litecoin miners.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The lower-end unit gets around $16 per day, while the A6+ gets $31 per day in profit. Owners of Scrypt mining rigs don’t have to mine LTC either, as they can also mine dogecoin (DOGE), gamecredits (GAME), and verge (XVG).
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Behind all the profits stemming from mining rigs that produce coins from algorithms like Blake256R14, Ethash, Equihash, and Scrypt is SHA256. The SHA256 algorithm can mine bitcoin (BTC) but also coins like bitcoin cash (BCH) and bitcoinsv (BSV).
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Even though profits are lower for SHA256 devices, the number of SHA256 machines towers over the quantity of devices that mine alternative consensus algorithms. There are far more products and manufacturers that produce bitcoin miners, and the number of SHA256 machines surely eclipses all of the aforementioned mining rigs that leverage different mining rulesets combined.
  </p>
  
